  <header class="page-head">
    <div>
      <h1 id="title">Roadmap</h1>
      <div class="sub" id="meta">Loading…</div>
    </div>
    <a class="pill" id="board-btn" href="/">Back to the board</a>
  </header>
  <div class="bar-controls">
    <input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search id / title / description…" />
    <span class="rm-zoom">
      <button class="chip mini" id="zoom-out" type="button" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
      <span class="sync-text" id="zoom-level">100%</span>
      <button class="chip mini" id="zoom-in" type="button" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
      <button class="chip mini" id="zoom-reset" type="button">Reset view</button>
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="bar-filters">
    <span class="fgroup">
      <span class="flabel">Status</span>
      <span class="chips" id="status-chips"></span>
      <span class="fbulk"><button class="chip mini" id="status-all" type="button" title="Show every status">All</button><button class="chip mini" id="status-none" type="button" title="Hide every status">None</button></span>
    </span>
    <span class="fgroup msel" id="bucket-select">
      <span class="flabel">Buckets</span>
      <button class="chip msel-btn" id="bsel-btn" type="button" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false">Filter <span class="msel-count" id="bsel-count" hidden></span></button>
      <div class="msel-panel bsel-panel" id="bsel-panel" hidden>
        <ul class="msel-list" id="bucket-list" role="listbox" aria-multiselectable="true"></ul>
      </div>
    </span>
    <span class="fgroup msel" id="flag-select">
      <span class="flabel">Flags</span>
      <button class="chip msel-btn" id="fsel-btn" type="button" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false">Filter <span class="msel-count" id="fsel-count" hidden></span></button>
      <div class="msel-panel fsel-panel" id="fsel-panel" hidden>
        <ul class="msel-list" id="flag-list" role="listbox" aria-multiselectable="true"></ul>
      </div>
    </span>
    <span class="fhint">tip: drag to pan, scroll to zoom, or Tab in and use the arrow keys</span>
  </div>
  <div class="summary" id="summary"></div>
  <details class="rm-chains-box">
    <summary>Dependency chains</summary>
    <div id="rm-chains"></div>
  </details>
  <div class="rm-viewport" id="rm-viewport" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Roadmap plane: arrow keys pan, plus and minus zoom, 0 resets the view, Tab reaches the ticket cards">
    <div class="rm-plane" id="rm-plane"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="tip"></div>
  <details class="legend">
    <summary>How to read this roadmap</summary>
    <div class="legend-body">
      <p>
        Every ticket sits on one plane with two fixed axes. Across is time: the cycle a ticket is
        committed to, otherwise the forecast landing date of its milestone, otherwise Backlog at the far
        right. Down is dependency depth: wave 0 is work nothing blocks, wave 1 waits on wave 0, and so
        on, the same grouping the dependency waves use elsewhere. Tickets that would land in the same
        cell are packed into lanes, so no card ever covers another.
      </p>
      <p>
        Curved lines are blocking relations, drawn from the blocker to what it blocks. A line in the
        risk color runs backward, meaning the blocker sits at or after the ticket it blocks on the time
        axis. Hover or focus a card for its status, assignee, milestone, wave, relations, and the reason
        for any flag; the card itself only carries the ticket number, a flag glyph, and the estimate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dependency chains lists each connected group of blocking edges, worst first. A chain runs one
        ticket at a time, so its length is measured against the people who own it rather than the whole
        team: the points on its critical path are charged to each owner at that person's own velocity,
        and the sequential total is compared with the time left before the target of the latest
        milestone the chain reaches. A chain that cannot fit flags every ticket in it with chain risk.
        Most tickets in a real project depend on nothing at all, which is why the summary counts them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Filters match the board: search, status chips, a Buckets panel, and a Flags panel. Filters and
        the pan/zoom position are saved and written into the address bar, so a refresh or a shared link
        lands on the same view.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keyboard: Tab to the plane, then arrow keys pan (hold Shift for a bigger step), + and − zoom,
        and 0 resets. Tab again to reach the cards, arrow keys move between them, Enter opens the
        focused ticket in Linear, and Escape dismisses the detail card.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>
